# Public site core metadata (hard rule)

> **JSON-LD, Open Graph, Twitter cards, and the page meta description
> state the company and the products customers and partners look for.
> Image license fields stay, because Google requires them. They do not
> replace the product facts, and they do not point a picture at the
> wrong product. Do not add markup that does not name a product, a
> partner role, a contact, or a required image-license field.**

GPT 6 desktop follows the same steps in
`pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/website-and-ui/GPT6-INDEX-AND-IMAGE-TAGS-2026-10-10.md`
section 6. Indexing and image-license fields stay under
`public-site-index-and-image-tags.mdc`.

## What customers and partners look for

| Who | Fact the markup must carry |
| --- | --- |
| Every buyer | Analog Informatics Corporation (AIC). Support is support@analoginfo.com. Contact is https://analoginfo.com/contact. |
| Commercial and government buyers | AIC Enterprise Privilege Suite. It discovers, rotates, and propagates privileged credentials and controls privileged sessions, with temporary elevation and audit evidence. Page: https://analoginfo.com/capabilities. Quote: https://analoginfo.com/pricing. |
| Defense suppliers | AIC CMMC Complete. A packaged secure enclave for suppliers preparing for CMMC Level 1, Level 2, and Level 3, with workforce training and assessment records. Page: https://analoginfo.com/cmmc. Pricing: https://analoginfo.com/cmmc/pricing. |
| Partners | Managed Service Providers, resellers, ISVs and technology partners, and implementation service providers sell and deliver both products. Say that on partner pages. |

Use these ids when a node needs a reference:

- `https://analoginfo.com/#organization`
- `https://analoginfo.com/#enterprise-privilege-suite`
- `https://analoginfo.com/#cmmc-complete`

## Required shape

1. The homepage graph leads with a WebPage whose description names both
   products, then a SoftwareApplication for each product (name, url,
   one-sentence description, provider organization id, offer URL,
   audience). ImageObjects follow, and they stay short.
2. Open Graph and the meta description on the homepage name both
   products. `og:url` is that page's `https://analoginfo.com/...` URL.
   `og:site_name` is Analog Informatics.
3. A product page's SoftwareApplication includes the url and the
   one-sentence description. A name alone is not a product node.
4. An image `about` points at the product the picture shows. Assessment
   evidence points at AIC CMMC Complete. Console, elevation, and session
   pictures point at AIC Enterprise Privilege Suite.
5. Keep `license`, `acquireLicensePage`, and `creator` on every
   ImageObject. Point `creator` at the organization id.

## Do not add

- `SearchAction`, or any action, aimed at `/search`. That page is `noindex`.
- A second copy of a screenshot caption, width, height, or a nested
  organization inside every image.
- A SoftwareApplication that only has a name.
- A price in JSON-LD. Point `offers` at the pricing page.
- Schema from a "Generate schema markup" button.
- Markup that does not name a product, a partner role, a contact, or a
  required image-license field.

The site head and the site footer each stay at or under 50,000
characters. Put the two product nodes in the homepage page-head graph.
Do not push the site-wide head over the cap, and do not delete layout
CSS to make room. Do not Prettify. Do not click Advanced settings Save.
Publish production `analoginfo.com` only.

## Proof

Fetch the live homepage. Both product names and both product ids are in
the JSON-LD. The WebSite node has no `SearchAction`. The meta
description and `og:description` name both products. `og:url` is
`https://analoginfo.com/`. Image `about` values match the picture.
